# acc.merge(other) of Accumulator<T, 1> (milestone2.md, "The accumulator"): the running sums added,
# as add_1_1 (a node of the tree of the summation), and the sums of the magnitudes added, rounded to
# nearest. The counts are added in the header. Both accumulators are objects: nothing comes from the
# program.
kernel:        acc_merge_1
input:         s
input:         a
input:         v
input:         c
output:        t
output:        b
value:         s+v
requires:      nonneg a
requires:      nonneg c
ensures:       rounded t nearest
ensures:       error t R c=1/(1+u) k=1 t=0
ensures:       rounded b nearest value=a+c
min_precision: 1
source:        add_1_1 of two running sums, and the sum of the magnitudes (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        unverified
ieee:          spec
cone_exempt:   b, the sum of magnitudes, does not reach t: its claim is read where b is finite (an entry about an output group other than the first), and where b is +inf the mask ok of acc_radius_k is false

t = add(s, v)
b = add(a, c)
